IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sa-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Act, not copied from the encoding's own output.
-- Weekdays used below: 28 February 2026 is a Saturday, 1 March a Sunday, 2 March a Monday, 3 March a Tuesday,
-- 4 March a Wednesday, 10 March a Tuesday, 24 March a Tuesday, 1 July a Wednesday.
-- One case at least for every question; each states the facts a person in the seat would give.
-- A case outside the encoding asserts an explicit "not covered" value, NOTHING.

§ `Cases for the questions of a person with a time limit`

§§ `When an Act or a provision takes effect or ends`

-- s 27(1): an Act with no commencement provision comes into operation on the day of assent.
#ASSERT `On which day does my Act come into operation` FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
-- s 27(2): a Bill reserved for Her Majesty's assent is taken to be assented to on the day the assent is notified by proclamation in the State.
#ASSERT `On which day does my Act come into operation` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS Date 20 4 2026

-- s 27(3): one proclamation fixes the day.
#ASSERT `On which day does a proclamation bring my provision into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)
-- s 27(5): a later proclamation made before the fixed day amends the day.
#ASSERT `On which day does a proclamation bring my provision into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 12 2026)
-- s 27(5): a later proclamation made on the fixed day is not made before it, so the day stands.
#ASSERT `On which day does a proclamation bring my provision into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)

-- s 27(6): not brought in sooner, the second anniversary of assent.
#ASSERT `On which day does my provision come into operation if no proclamation has brought it in sooner` TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2028)
-- s 27(6): brought in before the second anniversary, that day.
#ASSERT `On which day does my provision come into operation if no proclamation has brought it in sooner` TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)
-- s 27(6): a proclamation after the second anniversary does not bring it in "before" that anniversary.
#ASSERT `On which day does my provision come into operation if no proclamation has brought it in sooner` TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 6 2028) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2028)
-- s 27(7): the provision says section 27(6) does not apply; no proclamation yet, so the text gives no day.
#ASSERT `On which day does my provision come into operation if no proclamation has brought it in sooner` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: assent on 29 February 2024; the text does not say what the second anniversary of that day is.
#ASSERT `On which day does my provision come into operation if no proclamation has brought it in sooner` TRUE FALSE (Date 29 2 2024) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 28: in operation from the beginning of the commencement day.
#ASSERT `Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about` (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 7 2026) 0 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about` (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 30 6 2026) 23 EQUALS FALSE
-- s 4 "day": a day is 24 hours ending at the stroke of midnight, which is the instant the next day begins.
#ASSERT `Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about` (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 30 6 2026) 24 EQUALS TRUE
-- s 30: continues to have effect until the end of the specified day.
#ASSERT `Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) 12 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) 1 EQUALS FALSE
-- The stroke of midnight that ends the specified day: the encoding reads "until the end of the day" as excluding that instant (see the fork register).
#ASSERT `Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) 24 EQUALS FALSE

-- s 32(2)(d): a right accrued under a repealed Act is not affected by the repeal.
#ASSERT `Does the repeal, amendment or expiry affect what I have under the Act` TRUE `a right, interest, title, power or privilege created, acquired, accrued, established or exercisable, or a status or capacity existing, under it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 32(2)(e): nor a penalty incurred.
#ASSERT `Does the repeal, amendment or expiry affect what I have under the Act` TRUE `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, imposed, created or incurred, or liable to be, under it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 32(2)(a): nor does it revive anything not in force.
#ASSERT `Does the repeal, amendment or expiry affect what I have under the Act` TRUE `reviving anything not in force or existing at that time` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: nothing has been repealed, amended or expired; section 32 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Does the repeal, amendment or expiry affect what I have under the Act` FALSE `something else a repeal, amendment or expiry might touch` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Counting my period`

-- s 44(1) item 2 and s 4 "year": 3 years from 16 July 2025, counted as three years in turn, end on 15 July 2028.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` `begins at, on or with a specified day` (Date 16 7 2025) years 3 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2028)
-- s 44(1) item 3: begins from an event on 10 March 2026 (a Tuesday), so the first day counted is 11 March and 14 days end on 24 March.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` (Date 10 3 2026) days 14 EQUALS JUST (Date 24 3 2026)
-- s 44(1) item 6: after 15 January 2026, so the first day counted is 16 January; item 8: 2 months end immediately before 16 March.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` `begins after a specified day` (Date 15 1 2026) months 2 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2026)
-- s 44(1) item 8: the first day counted is 30 December 2025; there is no 30 February, so the period ends at the end of February.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` (Date 29 12 2025) months 2 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- Not covered: the text does not say what a week is.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` `begins at, on or with a specified day` (Date 1 3 2026) weeks 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: a period expressed to begin "from a specified day"; the text does not say how it is counted.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` `begins from a specified day` (Date 1 3 2026) days 14 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 44(2): one month from an event on 31 January 2026 (a Saturday) ends on 28 February 2026, a Saturday; the next business day is Monday 2 March.
#ASSERT `On which day is the last I may do the thing` `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` (Date 31 1 2026) months 1 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- s 44(2): Monday 2 March is a public holiday, so Tuesday 3 March.
#ASSERT `On which day is the last I may do the thing` `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` (Date 31 1 2026) months 1 (Date 2 3 2026) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 3 3 2026)
-- s 44(2): the last day, Tuesday 24 March 2026, is already a business day.
#ASSERT `On which day is the last I may do the thing` `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` (Date 10 3 2026) days 14 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 24 3 2026)
-- Not covered: a period of weeks.
#ASSERT `On which day is the last I may do the thing` `begins at, on or with a specified day` (Date 1 3 2026) weeks 2 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 4 "business day": not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday.
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about a business day` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about a business day` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about a business day` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about a business day` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) 1 EQUALS FALSE
-- A run of three public holidays from Monday 2 March covers Wednesday 4 March; Thursday 5 March is outside it.
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about a business day` (Date 4 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) 3 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about a business day` (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) 3 EQUALS TRUE

-- s 44(1) items 4, 5 and 7.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end if it runs up to a day the law names` `continues until a specified day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS Date 30 6 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end if it runs up to a day the law names` `ends at, on or with a specified day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS Date 30 6 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end if it runs up to a day the law names` `ends before a specified day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS Date 29 6 2026

-- s 44(1) item 1: a period occurring between 2 days includes both days.
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about one of the days of a period between two days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about one of the days of a period between two days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about one of the days of a period between two days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about one of the days of a period between two days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I ask about one of the days of a period between two days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS FALSE

-- s 44(3): required, and no period given: as soon as is reasonably practicable.
#ASSERT `Must I do the thing as soon as is reasonably practicable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I do the thing as soon as is reasonably practicable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I do the thing as soon as is reasonably practicable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 49(1): the beginning of the anniversary of the date of birth.
#ASSERT `On which day do I attain a particular age` (Date 15 6 2000) 18 EQUALS Date 15 6 2018
-- s 49(2): born on 29 February; 2018 is not a leap year, so the beginning of 1 March; 2020 is a leap year.
#ASSERT `On which day do I attain a particular age` (Date 29 2 2000) 18 EQUALS Date 1 3 2018
#ASSERT `On which day do I attain a particular age` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 EQUALS Date 29 2 2020

-- s 50: 2307 cents rounds down to 2305; an exact multiple stays.
#ASSERT `What amount must I pay after the amount is rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 2307 EQUALS JUST 2305
#ASSERT `What amount must I pay after the amount is rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 2305 EQUALS JUST 2305
#ASSERT `What amount must I pay after the amount is rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` FALSE 2307 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Having a document served on me, or serving one`

-- s 51(2)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii), (c): an individual.
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me, an individual, in this way` `delivering it to the individual personally` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me, an individual, in this way` `posting it to the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me, an individual, in this way` `leaving it at the place of residence or a place of business of the individual last known to the server` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me, an individual, in this way` `leaving it at the place of residence or a place of business of the individual last known to the server` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me, an individual, in this way` `another way of serving an individual` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 51(3): a body corporate.
#ASSERT `May a document be served on my body corporate in this way` `posting it to the registered office of the body corporate` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on my body corporate in this way` `posting it to a place of business of the body corporate last known to the server` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on my body corporate in this way` `another way of serving a body corporate` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 51(4): properly addressing, prepaying and posting as a letter.
#ASSERT `Was my document posted to the address` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was my document posted to the address` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 51(5): taken to be effected when delivered in the ordinary course of post, unless the contrary is proved.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` (Date 12 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST (Date 12 3 2026)
#ASSERT `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` (Date 12 3 2026) TRUE (Date 14 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2026)
-- s 52: a form to the same effect is sufficient provided that deviations are not calculated to mislead.
#ASSERT `Is the form I used sufficient` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the form I used sufficient` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: no form is prescribed or approved.
#ASSERT `Is the form I used sufficient` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Penalties and fees`

-- s 53(2)(a): an increase applies only to offences committed after it takes effect (at the beginning of 1 July 2026, section 28).
#ASSERT `Does a changed penalty apply to my offence` `the penalty is increased` (Date 2 7 2026) 10 (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 3 7 2026) 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a changed penalty apply to my offence` `the penalty is increased` (Date 30 6 2026) 23 (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 3 7 2026) 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 53(2)(b): a reduction extends to an earlier offence if the penalty is imposed after it takes effect.
#ASSERT `Does a changed penalty apply to my offence` `the penalty is reduced` (Date 30 6 2026) 23 (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 3 7 2026) 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a changed penalty apply to my offence` `the penalty is reduced` (Date 30 6 2026) 23 (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) 23.5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: a reduction and an offence committed after it takes effect; paragraph (b) speaks only of earlier offences.
#ASSERT `Does a changed penalty apply to my offence` `the penalty is reduced` (Date 2 7 2026) 10 (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 3 7 2026) 9 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 54: the standard scale. Imprisonment in months, a fine or fee in dollars.
#ASSERT `What is the standard penalty or fee for a division` 6 fine EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `What is the standard penalty or fee for a division` 6 imprisonment EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `What is the standard penalty or fee for a division` 12 `expiation fee` EQUALS JUST 30
-- Not covered: the table has no Division 9 imprisonment row.
#ASSERT `What is the standard penalty or fee for a division` 9 imprisonment EQUALS NOTHING
